    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "sound",
      "title": "Dead syllables: class and length decide",
      "text": "ปวด, ปาก and นก end in a stop (t, k): they are dead syllables, cut off short. The class of the first letter decides the tone. On mid-class ป they are low (ปวด, ปาก). On low-class น a short dead syllable is high (นก) and a long one is falling (นาก). Spell it out slowly the first time and you will begin to hear which word a tone belongs to.",
      "explains": [
        "th.practice.dead-syllables"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
